rule alarm v1
description "How an alarm climbs on what its sensor says: a noise raises it a level, a quiet moment lowers it from alert, and a siren stays on. An example written for the purpose of what a file's claims leave open"

enum level = calm | alert | siren
enum signal = quiet | noise

inputs
  level  : level
  signal : signal

outputs
  next_level : level

table step
policy unique
| level | signal | -> next_level |
| calm  | quiet  | level         |
| calm  | noise  | alert         |
| alert | quiet  | calm          |
| alert | noise  | siren         |
| siren | -      | level         |

machine alarm over step
  carry   level -> next_level
  initial calm
